  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "This is a rich and timely topic. Here is a comprehensive overview of the hotel brands an owner should consider when evaluating branded residences as part of a hotel project in the Caribbean and Latin America (CALA):\n\n---\n\n# Hotel Brands to Consider for Branded Residences in the Caribbean & Latin America\n\n\nBranded residences have become another vehicle for global hotel brands to increase their presence in CALA, and they have become an integral component of several new resort developments in Mexico and the Caribbean.\n \nAccording to panelists at the 2025 Caribbean Hotel Investment Conference & Operations Summit, providing branded residences is a win-win scenario for owners who can see a faster return on investment with buyers coming in on the rental units.\n\n\n\nTwo big segment growth areas for the entire Caribbean are all-inclusives and branded residences.\n Below is a breakdown of the most relevant brands by tier:\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 Tier 1: Large Multi-Brand Groups with Strong CALA Pipelines\n\n### 1. **Marriott International**\nMarriott is the leader in the branded residences space globally. \nMarriott International maintains continued leadership in branded residences across the Americas, including significant growth in Caribbean and Latin America markets.\n \nHugo Mirabal, director of feasibility and development at Marriott International, noted that branded residences are extremely important as leverage in the luxury development process, and that nine of the ten projects he is working on will include branded residences.\n\n\nKey brands in the region include:\n- **Ritz-Carlton Reserve** – \nMarriott's pipeline includes Cotton Bay, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve and Residences in Eleuthera, Bahamas, expected to open in 2029.\n\n- **Bvlgari Resort & Residences** – \nAlso in the pipeline is Bvlgari Resort & Residences in Cave, Exuma, Bahamas, expected in 2029.\n\n- **St. Regis** – \nSt. Regis Hotels & Resorts opened the St. Regis Cap Cana Resort in the Dominican Republic in Spring 2025, marking the first and only St. Regis in that country.\n\n- **Autograph Collection** – active in the Caribbean, including Barbados.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Hilton**\n\nHilton ended 2025 with record growth across the Caribbean and Latin America, topping 300 operating hotels in 35 countries and territories, fueled by strong demand for luxury and lifestyle resorts and residences.\n\n\nKey luxury brands with a residences focus include:\n- **Waldorf Astoria** – \nWaldorf Astoria Residences Costa Rica debuted in 2025, and the company signed Waldorf Astoria Residences Guadalajara — the first standalone Waldorf Astoria branded residences in the Caribbean and Latin America — featuring one-to-four-bedroom homes.\n\n- **LXR Hotels & Resorts** – \nHilton also signed a new ultra-luxury resort and residences in Manuel Antonio, Costa Rica, which will offer 170 guest rooms and one- to four-bedroom homes and is slated to join the LXR Hotels & Resorts collection in 2029.\n\n- **Conrad Hotels & Resorts** – \nThe pipeline includes Conrad Los Cabos in Mexico, and two new Conrad hotels have been signed to anchor Hilton's presence in key urban markets, including Conrad Lima planned for 2028.\n\n- **Curio Collection** – active in the Dominican Republic and Colombia.\n\n\nHilton plans to continue expanding its luxury portfolio including Waldorf Astoria, Conrad Hotels & Resorts, and LXR Hotels & Resorts, aiming to nearly double its presence across these three brands in CALA.\n\n\n---\n\n### 3. **IHG Hotels & Resorts**\n\nIHG reaffirmed its commitment to growth across Mexico, Latin America and the Caribbean, with nearly 400 open and pipeline properties throughout the region spanning every segment, and expects to add 32 hotels spanning its six luxury segment brands in the coming years.\n\n\nKey brands include:\n- **Six Senses** – \nVijesh Patel, director of development at Six Senses, said that offering branded residences is more than just a bonus — it is a requirement, especially in the ultra-luxury world, with deals at $3 million-plus per key where leveraging residential capital is critical.\n \nRecent openings include Six Senses La Sagesse Grenada.\n\n- **Kimpton Hotels & Restaurants** – \nIHG has a forthcoming joint Kimpton hotel and residence offering in Tulum, Mexico.\n\n- **InterContinental**, **Hotel Indigo**, and **Vignette Collection** are also expanding in the region.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Hyatt Hotels Corporation**\n\nThe Destination by Hyatt brand is a diverse collection of independent hotels, resorts, and residences offering one-of-a-kind experiences, and is expanding its footprint in Latin America and the Caribbean.\n Hyatt's branded residences division (led globally by Tina Necrason, Global Head of Branded Residential) is actively growing in the region, with brands including **Park Hyatt**, **Andaz**, and **Grand Hyatt**. \nFor example, Andaz Turks and Caicos on Grace Bay includes 59 hotel rooms and 74 branded residences, underscoring the project's strong real estate focus.\n\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 Tier 2: Ultra-Luxury & Boutique Brands\n\nThese brands command the highest price premiums and are particularly attractive for owners targeting the ultra-high-net-worth buyer segment:\n\n### 5. **Four Seasons**\nFour Seasons has a well-established presence in the CALA branded residences market. \nFour Seasons projects in the region feature world-class amenities and collections of branded residences — for example, a Caribbean development features 24 Four Seasons branded residences ranging from 2- to 4-bedrooms, with prices starting at $4.5 million.\n \nFour Seasons maintains a strong position as a single-brand operator globally in the branded residences sector.\n\n\n### 6. **Rosewood Hotels & Resorts**\n\nRosewood remains very active at the luxury end of branded residences.\n \nRosewood is considered among the most exciting five-star hotel brands in 2026, with Rosewood Hong Kong named the No. 1 hotel in the world in 2025, and Rosewood São Paulo, London, and Las Ventanas in Los Cabos all making the World's 50 Best Hotels list.\n \nRosewood is among the ultra-luxury brands developing within the Exuma Cays in the Bahamas.\n\n\n### 7. **Aman**\n\nAman continues to define the ultra-luxury segment globally in branded residences.\n \nAman is also developing within the Exuma Cays, alongside Rosewood and Bvlgari, making the Bahamas one of the most concentrated ultra-luxury branded residential markets in the region.\n \nThe presence of three ultra-luxury brands developing simultaneously within one archipelago is without precedent in the Bahamas.\n\n\n### 8. **Fairmont (Accor)**\n\nNew 5-star residential resort developments from Fairmont are setting a new standard for super-luxury in Latin America and the Caribbean.\n Fairmont Residences Mayakoba in Mexico is one of the flagship examples of this brand's residential ambitions in the region. \nAccor leads in scale globally, supported by a multi-brand portfolio exceeding 35 brands.\n\n\n### 9. **Mandarin Oriental**\n\nMandarin Oriental is positioned just outside the top tier globally, with a strong luxury presence.\n The brand has been active in branded residences development globally and is increasingly relevant in Latin American markets.\n\n### 10. **Montage Hotels & Resorts**\n\nMontage is among the brands setting a new standard for super-luxury residential resort development in Latin America and the Caribbean.\n \nMontage Cay, the brand's first private island development, spans 53 acres in the Abacos (Bahamas) and comprises 50 all-suite accommodations, including a collection of overwater bungalows.\n\n\n### 11. **Auberge Resorts Collection**\n\nAuberge continues to define the ultra-luxury segment in branded residences globally.\n The brand has a growing presence in Mexico and the Caribbean, particularly in resort destinations.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Key Takeaways for Owners\n\n| Brand Group | Flagship Brands for Residences | Best Fit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | Ritz-Carlton Reserve, Bvlgari, St. Regis | Ultra-luxury, island resorts |\n| **Hilton** | Waldorf Astoria, LXR, Conrad | Ultra-luxury to upper-upscale |\n| **IHG** | Six Senses, Kimpton | Wellness-focused, lifestyle |\n| **Hyatt** | Park Hyatt, Andaz, Destination by Hyatt | Lifestyle, resort communities |\n| **Four Seasons** | Four Seasons | Consistent luxury, proven sales |\n| **Rosewood** | Rosewood | Cultural luxury, high design |\n| **Aman** | Aman | Exclusivity, ultra-high-net-worth |\n| **Accor** | Fairmont, Raffles | Large resort communities |\n| **Montage / Auberge** | Montage, Auberge | Boutique ultra-luxury |\n\n\nA key finding from the Savills Branded Residences Report for the Americas is that branded residences command an average 36% brand premium (vs. a global average of 33%), underlining the financial value of choosing the right brand partner.\n \nThe expansion of branded residences is largely driven by the ability to diversify investment within a project — the upfront cash flow from residence sales helps make large-scale developments feasible, while the ongoing rental pool income creates an attractive long-term revenue stream.\n\n\nUltimately, the right brand will depend on the project's target buyer profile, price point, location, and the owner's appetite for brand standards and fees. Engaging a hotel advisory firm with deep CALA expertise is strongly recommended before committing to a flag.",
